            "review_title": "Review at Schiller River Club",
            "review_text": "Rob Nesbit\nWarsaw, Poland6958 contributions\n0\nGive it a pass.\nNov 2022\nInteresting place\nCame here on a Saturday night, not as full as could be, but still a few people around. Was a DJ playing some pretty good chill- out music, and the views from where we were sitting, near the river, were great.\nWhat I didn't like, was the list of a few rules at entrance, how very welcoming, or at least that is the impression I got from my Vietnamese friend.\n\nI also didn't like the fact that I had to go up and order my own drinks.....now you might say I am a lazy old bugger, and you are right, ha, but with the setting and the small amount of people in the bar, its not going to take much for a friendly bar man to wander around, clean tables, chat to customers, and take orders....its what makes a bar welcoming, and its not a big ask. But the bar man wasn't the friendliest outgoing person in the world so perhaps maybe not!\n\nThe beer, in any case, was a bit off......so were the cocktails, and the less said about my coca cola vodka the better - more coke than vodka! (i ordered vodka and coke. not coke and vodka!) \n\nHas a hippy style stage, and its a nice and relaxing place.......it has the presence of a good place just lacks that human touch.....(bit like most \"eco friendly people!\")\n\nGive it a pass...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 11, 2022",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
